# HestiaRE: keep the Docker repo from becoming a channel for unrelated software (#389).
#
# Deny list, not an allow list. A `Package: *` pin on this origin overrides any
# specific-package stanza regardless of order or quoting (measured on apt/deb13), so the
# allow-list form silently pins docker-ce itself to -1 and blocks its security updates.
# Named packages work, hence this shape.
#
# This NARROWS, it does not bound: a name list cannot cover packages Docker adds later.
# Revisit when the repo's contents change. A complete boundary is not expressible here -
# without the wildcard everything from the origin gets the default 500.
#
# It is not protecting against shadowing: no OS package shares a name with this repo.
# Debian/Ubuntu carry containerd, docker.io, docker-cli, docker-compose, docker-buildx;
# the repo carries containerd.io, docker-ce*, and the *-plugin variants.
Package: cagent docker-model-plugin docker-secrets-engine docker-secrets-engine-plugins
Pin: origin download.docker.com
Pin-Priority: -1
